# flo-halium: keep udev away from the loop devices while the APEX images are attached.
#
# The container's start attaches about a dozen APEX images to loop devices (mount-android.sh, and apexd in the
# container). On the 3.4 kernels the loop driver can hang when udev opens a loop device (to probe it, or because
# of its inotify watch) while another process is attaching one: the mounts of some APEXes then never finish.
# Found on the Nexus 5 and the SM-T520, which use this rule; this tree has the same loop driver.
SUBSYSTEM=="block", KERNEL=="loop[0-9]*", ENV{UDEV_DISABLE_PERSISTENT_STORAGE_RULES_FLAG}="1", OPTIONS+="nowatch"
